  What is Linux?
  Linux is an operating system just like windows,macos..
  
  An operating system helps us interact with the computer
  and manage things such as:
  
  Files and folders
  programs and applications
  memory
  hardware
  users and permissions
  
  Linux is widely used in:
  
  Servers
  cloud computing
  software development
  networking
  Cyber security
  Embedded systems
  
  .........................................................
  
  What is Linux terminal?
  
  In windows, we often use a grafical interface to create folders, delete files etc
  In Linux, we can perform these operations using the terminal
  
  The terminal allows us to communicate with the operating system by typing commands
  
  ..........................................................
  
  Commands:
  
  ...........................
  
  PWD: present working directory
  
  command: pwd
  
  It will tell us the directory in which we are currently working
  
  .....................................
  
  ls (list)

  this command display the contents (files,dir's..) in the curent working
  
  .................................
  
  How to create a directory?
  
  Syntax: mkdir <dir-name>
  
  ex: mkdir batch14
  
  ..............................
  
  How to create a multiple dir's?
  
  Syntax: mkdir <dir1> <dir2> <dir3>
  .........................
  
  How to create a dir inside a dir (how to create a child dir inside a parent dir)
  
  Syntax: mkdir <dir1>/<dir1>
  
  ex: mkdir batch14/rk
  
  Above command will create a rk dir inside batch14 dir
  ...........................
  
  Note: If we dont have parent dir and if we want to  create a parent dir and
  child dir inside parent dir then -p option should be used
  
  Syntax: mkdir -p <parent-dir>/<child-dir>
  
  ......................................
  
  How to delete the directory?
  
  Syntx: rmdir <dir-name>
  
  ...........................
  
  How to delete a dir and its content recursively?
  
  syntax: rm -r <dir-name>
  
  ......................................
  
  Tree command:
  
  Tree command is used to display the content of pwd
  in a tree like format
  .......................
  
  clear:
  
  This command will clears the terminal screen
  
  ..............................
  
  How to create a file?
  
  Touch command is used to create a file
  
  Synatx: touch <file-name>
  
  Ex: touch file1.txt
  
  .......................
  
  How to create a multiple files using touch command?
  
  syntax: touch <file1> <file2> <file3>
  
  ...............................
  
  How to delete a file?
  
  Syntax: rm <file-name>
  
  ..................................
  
  How to delete multile files together?
  
  Synatx: rm <file2> <file2> <file3>
  
  .................................
  
  cd: change directory
  
  It is used to navigate to given dir
  
  ex: cd batch14
  
  ...........................
  
  How to move back to previous dir?
  cd ..
  
  How to go back to 2 dir's backward
  
  cd ../..
  
  .................................
  
  Man
  
  ex: man <command-name>
  
  man mkdir
  
  Above command will open the manual page of mkdir (details of mkdir)
  
  
